content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-102 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-19870, filtered-water line",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical-seal leakage: the report describes a steady drip of approximately one drop per second. No numerical allowable leakage rate is documented. The applicable manual troubleshooting row is 'Leakage at shaft seal', which directs replacement of the mechanical seal under section 5.2 and an alignment check under section 5.4.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end vibration: Figure 3 is the applicable HF-300 criterion for vibration velocity measured on bearing housings, expressed in mm/s RMS. If the reported 2.1 mm/s is an RMS velocity reading, it is within Zone A, 0.0 to 2.8 mm/s RMS, and is 0.7 mm/s below the Zone A/B boundary at 2.8 mm/s. It is below Zone C, 4.5 to 7.1 mm/s, and below the Zone D threshold of 7.1 mm/s, where damage is likely and the figure says to stop the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration monitoring coverage is incomplete: the manual requires weekly measurement on both bearing housings and classification of the highest reading. Only the drive-end reading is supplied, so 2.1 mm/s can be compared with Figure 3 for that housing but cannot be confirmed as the pump's highest reading.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end housing temperature: the manual specifies that bearing temperatures are measured on the housing surface and gives limits of normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C, and trip at 90 C. The reported 66 C is within the normal range: 4 C below the normal upper limit, 14 C below alarm, and 24 C below trip. This reading does not indicate high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Immediate-stop assessment: neither documented stop reference is reached by the reported readings. Vibration is below the 7.1 mm/s Zone D threshold and temperature is below the 90 C trip. This does not defer the active seal leak indefinitely: the troubleshooting action remains planned seal replacement and alignment checking, and the pump must never run dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Leading cause to investigate: worn or cracked mechanical-seal faces. These are the first documented probable causes listed for leakage at the shaft seal; removal and replacement are required to confirm and correct the fault.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Second documented possibility: the seal has run dry. The HF-300 uses Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and must never run dry, so flush/dry-running history should be checked when investigating the leakage.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Third documented possibility: shaft misalignment. The seal-leakage troubleshooting row specifically requires an alignment check; use the manual's laser-alignment tolerances when carrying out that check.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Planning hold before field work starts: obtain the complete Westfield SSP-07 Rev 3 control list and add every control applicable to this task to the work order. The supplied extract establishes that SSP-07 applies to this pump but does not contain its controls.",
      "citations": [
        "C14"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before concluding the cause, record the available seal-flush and dry-running evidence. The specified arrangement is Plan 11 flush from pump discharge, and the pump must never be run dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before beginning mechanical-seal replacement.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly. The rotating assembly can be removed without disturbing the casing or pipework; the back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg and lifting equipment is required.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the impeller nut and impeller in accordance with mechanical-seal replacement section 5.2.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Withdraw the existing seal and sleeve and inspect the sleeve for scoring. If scoring is found on this serial, obtain the applicable acceptance/replacement criterion before deciding whether HF3-455 must be replaced; do not automatically apply the bulletin threshold intended for HF3-22000 and above.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit one new HF3-450 component mechanical seal and one new HF3-120 casing gasket. HF3-450 remains the specified seal for pumps below serial HF3-22000, including P-102.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reassemble and tighten all disturbed fasteners to manual Table 5 with lightly oiled threads: M16 casing bolts to 210 Nm; M24 impeller nut to 160 Nm; M10 seal gland nuts to 25 Nm; and M12 bearing-housing bolts to 85 Nm if disturbed. The 30 Nm cartridge-seal torque in SB-2026-014 does not apply to this serial.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check shaft alignment as required for shaft-seal leakage. Perform laser alignment after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, and achieve parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular alignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For return to service, maintain the Plan 11 flush arrangement and never run the pump dry; verify that the shaft-seal leakage corrective action has been completed. Resume the documented weekly vibration check on both bearing housings and classify the highest reading with Figure 3.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450",
      "description": "Mechanical seal, component type; applicable to P-102 because serial HF3-19870 is below HF3-22000",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; fit new during seal replacement and replace whenever the casing is opened",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Westfield SSP-07 Rev 3 applies because P-102 is a site pump. Its full applicable controls must be listed on the work order, but those controls are absent from the supplied evidence; the planning hold in the tasks must be cleared before work starts.",
      "citations": [
        "C14"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before carrying out mechanical-seal replacement.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Use lifting equipment for the back pull-out assembly; its documented mass is 68 kg.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Maintain the specified Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical-seal replacement standard labour time: 4.0 hours with 2 technicians, equivalent to 8.0 technician-hours.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment standard labour time: 1.5 hours with 1 technician, equivalent to 1.5 technician-hours.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Combined standard allowance for seal replacement followed by alignment: 5.5 hours of sequential task time and 9.5 technician-hours. Bearing-replacement labour is not included in this work order.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal selection and gland torque: manual AQ-OM-300 Rev D identifies component seal HF3-450 and Table 5 specifies 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts. SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, instead specifies cartridge seal HF3-450B and 30 Nm, but its scope is HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above. P-102 is HF3-19870, below that range, and the bulletin explicitly says pumps below HF3-22000 continue to use HF3-450 and manual Table 5. Decision: use HF3-450 and 25 Nm, not HF3-450B and 30 Nm; the later bulletin date does not override its serial-range restriction.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sleeve inspection and scoring limit: the manual requires inspection of the withdrawn sleeve for scoring but supplies no numerical rejection limit. The bulletin's requirement to replace HF3-455 when scoring exceeds 0.1 mm appears within the instructions 'On these pumps', meaning serial HF3-22000 and above. Decision: inspect P-102's sleeve, but do not treat 0.1 mm as the documented rejection limit for HF3-19870; escalate for the applicable criterion if scoring is found.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Was the reported 2.1 mm/s drive-end vibration measured as RMS velocity, and what is the current non-drive-end bearing-housing reading? Figure 3 is an RMS criterion, while the manual requires both housings and classification of the highest reading. [C06][C07]",
    "What numerical shaft-sleeve scoring acceptance or replacement criterion applies to HF3-455 on serial HF3-19870? The manual only says to inspect for scoring, and the 0.1 mm bulletin criterion is within the instructions for HF3-22000 and above. [C10][C13]",
    "What are the complete SSP-07 Rev 3 controls applicable to this seal-replacement task? Only the procedure's scope and work-order requirement are supplied, so site safety coverage cannot be completed from this extract. [C14]",
    "Is there a site-specific allowable mechanical-seal leakage rate for this filtered-water service? The supplied troubleshooting document gives a symptom and corrective action but no numerical drops-per-second limit against which to compare the reported rate. [C09]",
    "What site priority definitions and required completion date apply? The evidence does not define P1/P2/P3. P2 is a provisional planning judgement for prompt planned repair of an active leak where the reported vibration and temperature do not meet immediate-stop criteria. [C02][C07][C09]"
  ]
}
